<p>After a short stop in Dickinson, Roosevelt later wrote that “the whole town turned out with wild and not entirely sober enthusiasm. It was difficult to make them much of a speech as there were dozens of men each earnestly desirous of recalling to my mind some special incident.”</p>

<div class="image-gallery">
  <figure>
